# Design library

**Current notebook reading package:** [[Designs/CC History]] · [[Designs/Project Authority]] · [[Designs/CC Reference]] · [[Designs/Lab Progression]] · [[Amendments/README]]. [[Resources/Current Baseline]] distinguishes the maintained design checkout from captured M1 implementation snapshots.

[[Presentation Library/README|Presentation Library]] collects recurring talk, evidence, visual-density and review guidance. See [[Presentation Library/Preference and Source Register]] for what was directly requested, what is found in project source files, and the limits of the chat search.

Design is a first-class part of this notebook. This index connects current contracts, research proposals, previous designs, diagrams, and presentations without creating a second maintained copy of the product architecture.

## Current implementation design

| Area | Start here |
|---|---|
| Full M1 architecture | [Maintained design package](../../jiuwenswarm/docs/architecture/design-package/README.md) |
| CC responsibilities | [Capability capsules](../../jiuwenswarm/docs/architecture/design-package/2-capability-capsules.md) |
| Build order and acceptance | [Build plan](../../jiuwenswarm/docs/architecture/design-package/3-build-plan.md) |
| Design rationale and changes | [Recorded decisions](../../jiuwenswarm/docs/architecture/design-package/method/decisions.md) |
| Lab-related existing design | [Sidecar](../../jiuwenswarm/docs/architecture/design-package/development-tools/sidecar/README.md) and [RSI workbench](../../jiuwenswarm/docs/architecture/design-package/side-systems/rsi-workbench.md) |

## Your new design work

- [[Designs/cc-containerization-and-lab-isolation|Lab boundaries and CC containerization]] separates the infrastructure prototype from the CC packaging decision.
- [[Designs/skills-to-cc-mapping|Skills to CC mapping]] defines conversion and evaluation work, including Spec Kit as a capability hypothesis.
- [[Workstreams/Workload Characterization]] retains the open hardware-design question.

Use [[Templates/Design]] for new proposals. Promote accepted product/interface changes into the maintained package through the project process.

## Historical design and presentation lineage

| Collection | Why retain it | How to read it |
|---|---|---|
| [Capsule scratch/build repository](../../capsule-openjiuwen/INDEX.md) | CC schema derivation, reports, reviews, and early architecture | Historical research lineage; not current runtime authority |
| [RSI v0.2 designs](<../../RSI Design Docs>) | Previous RSI interfaces and workbench assumptions | Compare against current workbench contracts |
| [October planning](../../AI4Research_private_planning/2026-10-13-meeting-decisions.md) | Meeting rationale and scope evolution | Personal planning source |
| [Dated review outputs](../../outputs/m1-core-review-2026-10-14) | Frozen package comparisons and review deliverables | Compact package was retired; retain as a dated artifact |
| [Old Obsidian notes](../../tundle/obby/README.md) | Decisions, handoffs, and evolving intent | Historical context; some pointers are stale |
| [Slide exports](../../slides-png/README.md) | Visual history and source-deck mapping | Derived rasters, not editable design authority |
| [Paper2Agent presentation](../../jiuwenswarm/docs/research/paper2agent/presentation/README.md) | Current personal research presentation work | Research artifact; versions retain their own provenance |

Full file-level navigation, archived snapshots, and original locations are in [[Resources/Source Collections]]. [[Resources/review-batches/personal-collections-and-readiness|The source review]] records the exact files sampled and conflicts found; indexing a design does not validate all its claims.
